    "done_when": "docs/evidence/cut-cell-current-attribution/chord-rca/report.md answers four questions, each claim backed by a measurement on the CPU witness in place on the fleet allocation (TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, configure_dtypes before any array; main is at 2992599ff, which reverts the chord-membership merge). (1) Per-cell error decomposition of the diverted-single-null chord map at the analytic Solovev state at 132 realised cells: which cells carry the sup and the RMS, and booked minus analytic support current per cell, for at least the top ten cells. (2) The mechanism by which the reverted connected-separatrix membership (git show a59529f20, plus 9acda6b6d on top) moved weak-rotation-reactor-static chord sup from 9.54e-05 to 1.86e-02, at the cell level. (3) The true defect, or defects, stated as mechanisms, each with a falsifiable prediction that you test. Example: an oracle membership taken from the analytic separatrix and the analytic plasma region, substituted into chord booking, should drop the diverted sup to a stated value while leaving weak rotation at about 1e-4. Report the measured numbers and say which predictions failed. Read the prior evidence first: the S19 cell-64 diagnosis (9 of 25 samples below the saddle level that are not axis-connected), benchmarks/chord_booking_operation_trace.py, the diverted chord attribution and exact-support anchors in docs/evidence/archive/cut-cell-current-attribution-landed.html, docs/figures/cut-cell-current-attribution/chord-regression-attribution/attribution.md, and contour-tree-topology-authority section 5, which moves the chord clip's axis-connected membership onto the contour tree. (4) The recommended implementation, as one or more nodes each with a done-when, stating whether it rides on the contour tree (nova/equilibrium/contour_tree.py and contour_tree_mesh.py, now on main) or is independent. The report embeds poloidal panels that follow the AGENTS plotting rules: line contours on stated levels, both null sets with draw_nulls, the wall, and booked and analytic support cells marked. They are rendered by benchmarks/chord_private_flux_rca.py into docs/figures/cut-cell-current-attribution/chord-rca/ as PNG with SVG beside it (git add -f). No production source edits. Status complete, or blocked with a named blocker; in-progress is not a recognised status.",
